# PORT=8899
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...                  contribution graph + Dashboard → Stats; `repo` + `user:email` scopes to count private repos
# GITHUB_USERS=kostis4563             logins /api/github/contributions may look up (comma-separated); the token's own login always is
# Dashboard → Profile → "Add from Discord": the Discord application Supabase signs people in with (Developer Portal → OAuth2),
# with SITE_URL/api/discord/callback added to its redirects. Both unset = the route answers 503.
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=...
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# STATS_OWNER_EMAIL=you@example.com     optional: dashboard account allowed to see private repo names (else matched via the GitHub account's emails)
# STATE_DIRECTORY=/var/lib/blxr-search
# REVIEW_SALT=any-long-random-string
# SITE_OWNER_EMAIL=you@example.com     dashboard account allowed into Dashboard → Review panel and Logs (needs SUPABASE_URL + key below; defaults to STATS_OWNER_EMAIL)
# Account mail ("password changed" notice) — all four needed, else the route answers 503
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...                 sending-only key for blxr.net (same one Supabase's SMTP form uses)
# MAIL_FROM=blxr <no-reply@blxr.net>
# SITE_URL=https://blxr.net
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...        only for POST /api/account/delete (Settings → Delete account); leave unset to disable
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173  extra browser origins allowed to write, comma-separated (SITE_URL always is)
